SY_TALK("geTIFWA_qX4",[[0,["https: www.amruta.org/1982/04/02/shri-ramas-birthday-rama-navami-1982/"]],[0,["ETVD 2016-0424"]],[0,["TC BC 2017-0317"]],[10,["So first of all we’ll start talking about energies."]],[15,["These energies are moving"]],[20,["within us and how they activate"]],[23,["and we’ll talk about the third energy"]],[26,["which is the one which has evolved us"]],[29,["and that’s how we are here."]],[31,["And we’ll talk about your Self, the controlling part,"]],[36,["which is controlling you, the Spirit."]],[43,["So if you go on an abstract line,"]],[46,["it will be very appealing [?]  with it."]],[55,["Then afterwards, you see,"]],[57,["when we have talked about energies, this, that,"]],[60,["once the people- that is within you- you see,"]],[62,["sort of they’ll feel ego, this ego: “we have these energies"]],[65,["we can utilize these energies, do this, do that”"]],[68,["and then you’ll bring them down to Sahaja Yoga, later on."]],[71,["But to begin with, better talk of abstract."]],[75,["Because Indians are different, Western people are different,"]],[83,["they are fed up of religion, they are fed up of all this."]],[86,["So if you talk of religion, it gives, creates a problem."]],[91,["That’s why in the beginning, you see, Vedas, they were written down."]],[96,["They didn’t talk of God or Deities at all."]],[100,["They talked about God, God the Creator,"]],[103,["but just about Brahmadeva,"]],[105,["throughout Hiranyagarbha, Brahmadeva, right side they talked, you see."]],[110,["And the all thing is said, mantra is like :"]],[113,["“Bhur, Bhuvah, swaha”. 3 things. Now, Bhur is actually"]],[119,["the Mooladhara, is the earth upper it, the Mooladhara."]],[125,["Mooladhara chakra and Mooladhara itself."]],[127,["Then Bhuvah. Bhuvah is the one which is called the antariksha"]],[133,["[atmosphere, intermediate space], is the one which is all created,"]],[136,["in talks of Brahmadeva."]],[141,["Then swaha. Swaha is capacity to burn out,"]],[146,["of the agny [fire] you see?"]],[152,["It is so surprising and then they talk of mahatapa,"]],[157,["tapaha and maha. “Bhur, Bhuvah, swaha, maha tapa”."]],[165,["So when they talk of swaha, they talk of maha."]],[169,["Maha is what you call the great, Allah Hou Akbar, and of tapa."]],[178,["Tapa is the one where you have to become a tapasuy,"]],[183,["means a person who is going into penance, that of Christ."]],[191,["And they say that you have to penetrate through the Surya,"]],[196,["that is this. And the all thing is such an obstacle,"]],[201,["and then you get your moksha."]],[203,["So they have talked of all the chakras."]],[206,["But if you talk about the abstract part of it,"]],[208,["people have no objection, they listen to it,"]],[210,["listen as [inaudible] there’s no religion as such."]],[219,["Today specially I'm talking about the Vedas"]],[226,["and these havanas we do."]],[231,["When we do the havana it is a Yagnya."]],[239,["Yagnya means \"by which you know\". ‘nya’ means to know. Yagna."]],[244,["And this is done where you use 'Svaha' as the word."]],[250,["That means you use the principle of fire"]],[258,["to burn off all that is wrong in you, 'Svaha'."]],[265,["And you awaken it by taking the different names of the God."]],[272,["And it started at the time of Rama."]],[276,["Today is Ram Navami."]],[278,["I should say it was not started, we should say,"]],[281,["but it was very much invoked when Rama lived"]],[284,["and they used to do Yagnyas at that time."]],[288,["The reason was, the people had just started realizing"]],[294,["that there is something higher"]],[297,["and you have to worship that higher Self, the seers said,"]],[301,["and they thought that the best thing is to do Yagnyas."]],[309,["On the left side, of course, the people started the worship of God"]],[313,["and the dedication to God and all those things,"]],[315,["that is Bhakti , but mainly what they did"]],[321,["before Rama was the Yagnyas, the Vedas,"]],[328,["with which they prayed to different elements"]],[331,["- elements have made our chakras –"]],[334,["and tried to evoke the deities of the Elements."]],[339,["But actually it amounts to the same."]],[346,["So as a child, Rama was studying with a very great saint,"]],[357,["and when he was studying with him,"]],[363,["Vashishta was the name of the great saint."]],[367,["And Vashishta had an ashram where Rama and his brothers studied."]],[376,["Shri Mataji to a lady: come along, come in, come forward."]],[379,["Give her a chair to sit down. Can you, is there a seat here?"]],[383,["I think Gavin can go, lots of seats are there."]],[403,["Rama was studying with this Vashishta"]],[409,["and they used to come for holidays to father's place."]],[414,["Then, he had the capacity to kill a demon with only one arrow."]],[424,["It’s called as ekabani. One arrow was sufficient of Sri Rama."]],[428,["And he was a small little child, say about seven, eight years of age."]],[434,["And people were surprised how he could do it."]],[439,["So whenever they had a yagnya"]],[441,["– now these yagnyas were created to awaken, evoke, the Deities"]],[447,["inside the spinal chord – actually."]],[451,["And for these yagnyas they used to sit down"]],[454,["and do all these havanas the way we do it."]],[458,["But at that time, the rakshasas would come and try to spoil the yagnyas,"]],[463,["because yagnyas are to be done with pure heart"]],[468,["and with cleanliness and with purity, it should not be insulted,"]],[472,["there’s a protocol about it."]],[474,["While they thought that, “If we insult the Deities there,"]],[478,["then the Deities will disappear and their yagnyas will be spoiled.”"]],[482,["Now these yagnyas were done, in the olden times even, even when"]],[490,["Rama was not here. But at the time of Rama also,"]],[494,["there were some rakshasas"]],[496,["who took a special pleasure in spoiling these yagnyas"]],[501,["and Rama as a child would go and protect them from the demons."]],[507,["And the demons would take some sort of a funny form"]],[510,["and come like invisible creatures and put some bones"]],[520,["of animals and things like that in the yagnya."]],[523,["And that would spoil the effects of the yagnya."]],[528,["And Rama would protect that, as a child."]],[532,["Imagine, as a child he used to do that!"]],[535,["They would be doing the yagnya and he would be sitting outside"]],[538,["with all his small brothers around him"]],[542,["and they would kill the demons who would try to destroy the yagnyas."]],[547,["This is the early life of Rama in which you see"]],[556,["how, as a child also, he showed an amount of"]],[570,["expertise, you can say, in arrow and bow."]],[574,["So any time you see a statue"]],[578,["– how to make out a Shri Rama’s statue, is to see if there’s an arrow"]],[582,["and a bow, then its a Rama’s statue."]],[591,["Now his coming on this Earth,   gave us the development of the Right Side"]],[598,["and so the yagnyas were also on the Right Side."]],[602,["Because first of all when human beings came on this Earth,"]],[606,["they were frightened of all the animals who would invade them"]],[611,["and all kinds of horrible rakshasas and all those people,"]],[614,["and negative forces they would trouble them."]],[618,["So, in that state they needed to create a king, a ruler,"]],[625,["who was an ideal king and he would rule according to the laws of dharma."]],[631,["So He was the one in charge of that era,"]],[638,["what we call as Satya Yuga you can say, but actually,"]],[643,["He was here in Treta Yuga."]],[647,["That’s the time when He as here, that’s Treta Yuga,"]],[651,["and Krishna came at the lime of Dwapar Yuga."]],[655,["And today is the time, when I came it was Kali Yuga."]],[661,["But now, today, the time is of Krita Yuga,"]],[666,["the Yuga where work will be done: ‘Krita’ means, “work will be done”."]],[670,["This is the time where work will be done."]],[674,["So how things have moved from one to another?"]],[677,["Now in the Dwapar Yuga when Shri Rama came,"]],[681,["the idea of kingship and rulership started."]],[690,["So the greatest emphasis was on the goodwill of the people."]],[703,["The people had to have goodwill:"]],[707,["for the people and for the king, and for the betterment of humanity."]],[717,["The will, that is the Right Side."]],[720,["So how to create the goodwill in people?"]],[724,["First the leader has to sacrifice and show how far he can go"]],[731,["in sacrificing to keep the moral and the goodwill of the people."]],[738,["So the Right Side was created by the advent of Shri Rama"]],[741,["because he showed a path of creating among people the awareness"]],[751,["that they should be ruled, that they should not be anarchist,"]],[758,["there should be one head who should be able"]],[761,["to organize, co-ordinate and work out a collective thing."]],[771,["You see, when we think of a king we want to oust him"]],[776,["because we don’t like the idea of being ruled someone."]],[781,["Because he’s not a good king perhaps, o"]],[785,["or he doesn’t represent that will of the people"]],[789,["which is a common will which creates this king"]],[794,["who rules for the maintenance of that goodwill."]],[799,["It is a symbolic expression of your goodwill."]],[803,["So when you create a law, it is also the expression,"]],[808,["common expression, of all the common people,"]],[812,["of the common feeling that they should abide with law."]],[817,["It doesn’t come to you that you are a slave,"]],[824,["or you are to be dominated, or you have to be put down,"]],[827,["but it is only your common will, which is good."]],[831,["The desire of all the people which is the good, righteousness,"]],[844,["incarnates as Shri Rama and He looks after that will."]],[850,["Because, supposing an individual may start saying that,"]],[853,["“This is not good,” “This is not good.”"]],[856,["An individual might take a different attitude about things."]],[859,["But you must have some symbol of that goodness"]],[864,["placed onto someone."]],[867,["And those symbols were created to symbolize your righteousness,"]],[875,["your sense of good, so that you can be saved yourself!"]],[880,["Supposing, today, somebody comes and hits you. Alright?"]],[887,["Now you can feel how bad it is"]],[889,["to be hit by someone or murdered by someone,"]],[892,["so you decide there should be a law protecting you."]],[896,["But tomorrow you may do the same thing."]],[898,["So what you do is to take out your goodwill,"]],[904,["represent it as the kingdom or a king or a governing body."]],[913,["So, the government as it is represents,"]],[918,["should represent, also – in both ways."]],[922,["It’s not that it always represents."]],[923,["It may not at all represent, may not, possibly."]],[927,["But, that the government itself should represent the good in you,"]],[933,["the purity in you, the pure will to be good, to be protected."]],[938,["And that you also should abide by it. It’s a very mutual thing."]],[945,["But what happens that, once you start electing someone like that,"]],[949,["or making someone like that, or appointing someone like that,"]],[952,["as usual, he goes into an ego trip."]],[957,["[It’s] a simple thing like that. It’s absolutely a simple ego trip."]],[961,["The government gets into an ego trip,"]],[964,["people get amazed how people behave."]],[969,["They’ll elect, supposing, a Prime Minister"]],[973,["and suddenly you find the Prime Minister behaves like a brute"]],[976,["and you can’t understand – “We have elected somebody"]],[979,["like a Prime Minister thinking that he will do the good to us.”"]],[982,["You see. It’s possible."]],[983,["And then the revolutions take place while people revolt, fight it out."]],[989,["Again the will of the people fights it and makes it alright."]],[999,["So we have to have something absolute"]],[1003,["because all these values are changing every moment."]],[1008,["Isn’t it? We think that this government did not do so well"]],[1011,["– for example, we think like that – so we want to demolish this government."]],[1015,["Then we bring another one and we find the same thing happening."]],[1018,["See, whether you bring a communist or you bring a socialist"]],[1024,["or you bring a democrat or you have a monarchy,"]],[1029,["whatever you may have!"]],[1031,["But still, what happens actually is that,"]],[1034,["all these things that come up and go away…"]],[1040,["(aside: Gavin come here. Can you move forward a little bit so that everybody can be seated?)"]],[1046,["All these changes that take place"]],[1051,["go on creating a feeling in a man that we should be anarchist."]],[1059,["Why should we have any government? Why should we have any king?"]],[1065,["Why should [we] be ruled by anyone?"]],[1068,["Because you find the person who’s ruling is not up to the mark"]],[1074,["and he is just trying to deceive you."]],[1078,["At that point you have to have some absolute standards."]],[1084,["If you have an absolute standard then you can always judge"]],[1088,["that this king is deviating from the right path,"]],[1092,["is not doing what a king should do."]],[1095,["A king has to be like Rama. He has to be like Rama."]],[1100,["Representing your will, your goodwill,"]],[1105,["your sense of proper judgement, fair play and righteousness."]],[1113,["If the king is not righteous"]],[1115,["then your collective goodwill will go against the king."]],[1121,["Now you go and throwing one from another."]],[1123,["Say, I’ve seen now for example in France:"]],[1126,["We had one kind of a Prime Minister."]],[1131,["He did lots of things which were not good so he was thrown away."]],[1135,["So you had another one kind of one."]],[1137,["Now he’s doing another thing, so he’s going to be thrown away."]],[1140,["And we are just going, playing games you see."]],[1142,["First of all we have say, Labour Government. We don’t like it."]],[1146,["So then we have another Government, Conservative Government."]],[1148,["We don’t like it. Throw it away! Go on playing with it all the time."]],[1152,["But in this relativity we are improving – definitely."]],[1156,["We are more aware, understanding the value of these people,"]],[1162,["and also the public is understanding."]],[1165,["But then when too many such people come in who are negative,"]],[1174,["they also bring down the will, the collective will, very low."]],[1180,["And people start identifying themselves with these autocrats"]],[1188,["or those people who are ego-orientated, who have no moral values,"]],[1194,["who have no fear of God, who deny religion,"]],[1205,["who deny evolution"]],[1208,["and the Government starts behaving in such a manner"]],[1213,["that you are amazed – how this is the Government?"]],[1215,["Like in Chile and Argentina, the way the Government is behaving"]],[1219,["and is putting down the people."]],[1222,["All these things are happening. You don’t know."]],[1224,["It’s such a relative terminology."]],[1227,["Like El Salvador, you don’t know what to do over there now"]],[1230,["– whom to support. Whether to support the Americans,"]],[1233,["or to support the Russians and all that."]],[1236,["Now, under these circumstances a Sahaja Yogi can stand and say,"]],[1241,["“Now, what to do? Should we join this or that?”"]],[1246,["All is a wasteful thing. It’s just a game going on."]],[1249,["Let them break their heads. They are good for nothing. Useless people."]],[1253,["So you cannot solve these problems"]],[1256,["and you are not supposed to solve them."]],[1259,["They must get their Realisation and establish the Kingdom of God."]],[1264,["So [that] really Rama rules on this Earth"]],[1270,["and not these horrible kings who change their morality every day,"]],[1274,["who change their ideas every day,"]],[1276,["those whose will is sometimes for something materialistic."]],[1282,["Like I would say now in our country (UK)"]],[1285,["we thought that we’ll have Mrs. Thatcher."]],[1287,["Good, very good, she’s coming up well I should say,"]],[1290,["certain good things she is saying, like self-restraint and all that,"]],[1294,["those things she’s talking good things."]],[1296,["But what about herself following this!"]],[1300,["Shri Rama, not only propounded what was good but he followed that."]],[1305,["He sacrificed for that and he established his own symbol"]],[1309,["as a pure symbol of that righteous will,"]],[1313,["that is within the people, which is the collective righteous will."]],[1319,["Now, for example, you can see clearly"]],[1322,["how the ego oriented things work out, first of all,"]],[1325,["by the misidentifications we can have."]],[1327,["Now if you are a communist, you have to be out and out communist!"]],[1330,["You cannot have compromise between democratic methods and communism."]],[1334,["They can’t find any integration."]],[1336,["They think  if you have to be this you have to be absolutely this."]],[1339,["If you have to be that it has to be absolutely that."]],[1341,["But, in Sahaja Yoga, what you find is both are integrated"]],[1346,["because you have the complete capital and have now to distribute it."]],[1354,["This is a complete integration here."]],[1357,["All these ‘isms’ and all that are experiments of the artificial,"]],[1362,["of the mind, just a projection of the mind,"]],[1364,["which is, whatever [is] man-made is artificial, you know that."]],[1367,["But what is God made is all integrated."]],[1370,["That, whatever you have within yourself, you must give it to others."]],[1377,["Now see for administration also, what happens after Sahaja Yoga."]],[1382,["Say, I am your Mother, here, sitting down."]],[1386,["You like me to guide you. You like me to govern you."]],[1393,["You like me to correct you, you like me to scold you"]],[1397,["and to even go to a great extend to see that your life improves."]],[1404,["Supposing I say, “Alright, I give up. I don’t want to trouble you!”"]],[1408,["You will not like. None of you will like such a situation"]],[1411,["where I say, “Alright you are a gone case,"]],[1413,["I have nothing to do. You get out.”"]],[1415,["Nobody will like such a situation. You want me to govern you."]],[1419,["You want me to look after you. You like that."]],[1423,["Automatically you have started liking it."]],[1427,["There’s no domination, but you want my domination."]],[1430,["You want me to dominate you."]],[1432,["You want that all my desire should be dominated – automatically."]],[1436,["Why you feel that, “It is alright, it is very good"]],[1440,["if Mother takes interest in me, corrects me. It’s a privilege”?"]],[1444,["Why do you think like that?"]],[1447,["Because by that there is a general good created."]],[1454,["It’s a general good created in you."]],[1456,["Because you have become integrated."]],[1459,["Your body, your mind and your soul, all of them think the same way."]],[1469,["They all want the same. There’s no difference."]],[1473,["Once there is integration"]],[1475,["you will find that Sahaja Yoga is the easiest way to live it."]],[1479,["But if there is not, then it is no."]],[1481,["For example, if you are a lazy person, say for example,"]],[1484,["or you are a very hot-tempered person"]],[1487,["or you are a sort of a dual person,"]],[1495,["or you are playing tricks with yourself, you are playing games,"]],[1500,["then you won’t like Sahaja Yoga."]],[1503,["As long as these situations are in you,"]],[1507,["you will not like Sahaja Yoga."]],[1509,["But once this situation is overcome, then you will like it"]],[1515,["because then you will know that whatever is good for your Spirit"]],[1519,["is for the well-being of you all and of all the people."]],[1527,["Once this well-being comes in,"]],[1529,["everyone feels absolutely nourished and fresh."]],[1535,["So the governing part is enjoyable."]],[1544,["The correction part is even more enjoyable."]],[1547,["And that you are in the attention of your Mother"]],[1552,["is such a great feeling within yourself that,"]],[1555,["“Yes. No, nothing will go wrong with me. She’ll look after me.”"]],[1560,["“She’s there to look after me.”"]],[1562,["But this integration part comes very late because of ego problems."]],[1568,["You have built up egos because of"]],[1571,["wrong type of people administering you."]],[1574,["From your childhood you might have had bad parents"]],[1578,["who never talked of God, of good things of life."]],[1581,["They themselves did not lead a life of sacrifice."]],[1584,["Very self indulgent parents can create a problem like that."]],[1588,["They never gave you the right type of life,"]],[1591,["a proper value system which should have been there."]],[1594,["They never educated how to enjoy righteousness, virtues, in life."]],[1599,["Possibly, later on, the country in which you are born,"]],[1603,["the other people who surround you also might have done that."]],[1607,["Also, your government, whichever you have known, must have done that."]],[1611,["So when these things change, when you find that you have achieved"]],[1616,["that kind of integration within you:"]],[1619,["that whatever your body likes is good for your Spirit also."]],[1624,["Like say for example, I don’t like certain things myself."]],[1628,["I don’t like drinks, I don’t like it."]],[1632,["I just don’t like it. Nobody can tempt me."]],[1634,["I mean, no question of temptation, I just don’t like."]],[1637,["I will hate the things which are really bad for my Spirit"]],[1641,["– automatically. I don’t have to tell myself, it’s just there."]],[1645,["To tell lies I don’t like because it harms me there. I don’t like it."]],[1652,["Whatever is good for your Spirit will automatically work out"]],[1655,["as soon as this integration takes place"]],[1658,["and this is the work of Sahaja Yoga today."]],[1660,["That’s why I said it is Krita Yuga, is to be done."]],[1664,["And this integration must be achieved within ourselves."]],[1669,["So sometimes you have to make your body come to this level."]],[1674,["Maybe you are under the influence of some bhoots"]],[1677,["your body doesn’t help you."]],[1680,["Little bit of tapasvita, or penance,"]],[1683,["is needed after Sahaja Yoga to make this possible."]],[1687,["And then once you start enjoying it then you like it."]],[1693,["Like driving a car – in the beginning it’s difficult."]],[1696,["Or swimming, anything,"]],[1697,["when you try to do it’s rather difficult in the beginning."]],[1700,["If I say, “You forget it now, whatever"]],[1702,["you have done in the past you forget it now"]],[1704,["get to the new things now. You have to do it.”"]],[1707,["So you have to put your mind to it with all your full zest."]],[1714,["That, “Alright, if my body’s not helping me – alright –"]],[1718,["then I’ll try to improve the body because I’m not the body.”"]],[1721,["“If my mind is not helping me, I must improve my mind."]],[1725,["If my intellect is standing in the way"]],[1731,["I’ll have to put my intellect right"]],[1733,["because after all I have to be integrated."]],[1736,["If I am not integrated I’m not going to enjoy anything"]],[1739,["nor am I going to do anything good to myself or to others."]],[1743,["So why am I here? Why am I trying to destroy myself?”"]],[1747,["But when you are disintegrated, you will be surprised."]],[1750,["your one action will destroy your second action"]],[1754,["and second action will destroy third action – when you are disintegrated."]],[1758,["I’ll give you an example: Supposing now I am sitting here"]],[1761,["and somebody tells me that this will burn you."]],[1765,["This is my own maya. But the body wants to burn itself."]],[1771,["It says, “No, alright, don’t listen to this, just burn itself.”"]],[1775,["Now, when I say this it sounds absurd."]],[1777,["But, say, the mind says you should not take to alcohol,"]],[1783,["but still you’ll go to the pub, then you are disintegrated."]],[1789,["Gradually once you start listening to your body too much,"]],[1792,["your mind just gives in. It just gives in."]],[1795,["In every thing that you do, if you are integrated,"]],[1799,["you will be amazed that you will really become dynamic."]],[1804,["Integration is nothing but your complete connection with your Spirit."]],[1809,["The Spirit starts flowing into it."]],[1812,["In every walk of life you will be amazed how dynamic you’ll become"]],[1816,["if you are integrated."]],[1820,["Just the connection is to be absolutely achieved with your Spirit."]],[1827,["Whenever you think of something,"]],[1829,["“Is it good for my Spirit?”"]],[1832,["Some people have a habit of thinking that spiritual life is such"]],[1840,["that you hang by the shoestring somewhere, in the air"]],[1843,["and there is no connection to the day to day life."]],[1848,["So many people think like that."]],[1849,["They think such a man should be a thin, miserable creature"]],[1854,["hanging onto some tree or something"]],[1860,["and should be absolutely in a paranoid state or something."]],[1866,["That he is frightened of the whole world;"]],[1869,["who cannot talk to anyone,"]],[1871,["who is so much exclusive that he becomes a recluse."]],[1876,["These absurd ideas should to be given up by Sahaja Yogis."]],[1880,["You have to be very much there, absolutely there between all of them."]],[1886,["But something: you should be rare, a different type,"]],[1888,["a unique personality."]],[1890,["You are to be there with all these things that are going on."]],[1894,["Now people are frightened, you know, even of Sahaja Yogis."]],[1898,["They are frightened of Sahaja Yogis."]],[1900,["[If] they see somebody negative, they [say],"]],[1903,["“Oh, this thing, that thing.” Now take a fight with that person."]],[1907,["Take a fight. “How could you dare to do this, such a thing?"]],[1912,["You are a Sahaja Yogi! Come up! What do you mean by this?”"]],[1915,["You have to fight it out."]],[1918,["As long as possible you should try to salvage a person,"]],[1921,["talk to him in that manner."]],[1923,["The other side of it is that when you talk to others,"]],[1928,["when they come to you, then there has to be a kind"]],[1933,["of a tremendous sincerity within you."]],[1939,["If you are doing with that sincerity"]],[1941,["people will know you are doing with sincerity."]],[1944,["When you talk to a person they should know there’s sincerity"]],[1947,["your heart is there."]],[1951,["For example, you may talk to that person very sweetly,"]],[1953,["but your heart may not be there and the person might think,"]],[1956,["“Oh, he’s just seeking elections.”"]],[1959,["Alright? But if you talk to someone with the sincerity you’ll say,"]],[1962,["“How could you do such a thing? Can’t you see yourself?"]],[1966,["Can’t you work it out? That’s what it is. You are here for that.”"]],[1971,["Now in saying so, your sincerity, which is coming from your heart,"]],[1978,["is to be seen, and that’s what is Shri Rama’s character is:"]],[1983,["that he was on the right side of the heart,"]],[1987,["means the heart put to activity."]],[1992,["Do you understand that, where Kabira has said,"]],[1997,["“Mana mamata ko thira kara Lau.”"]],[2002,["“I will make my compassion of my heart – mana – from my heart,"]],[2008,["the compassion, make it steady. “aur pancha hi tattva milau,”"]],[2013,["“and put them into five elements.”"]],[2016,["You see, in the same way, when you are in the left heart,"]],[2020,["that’s your sincerity. It’s your heart-felt thing."]],[2024,["But the heartfelt thing, what’s the use?"]],[2026,["You see, there are many Sahaja Yogis who really feel,"]],[2029,["this world is horrible and something must be done,"]],[2032,["Sahaja Yoga must be brought in."]],[2034,["But how many of you are really putting that to action?"]],[2042,["Absolutely into action?"]],[2046,["Without that, your Rama’s tattwa cannot be improved."]],[2051,["Rama’s tattwa is only improved when"]],[2054,["you put all the things into action that exactly Shri Rama did."]],[2059,["So in the ascent of man, when he came up to Rama’s place,"]],[2063,["the advent of Rama was not in the centre, but on the right-hand side."]],[2067,["He moved aside. So much so, that he forgot about his past."]],[2072,["He’s never mentioned that He’s an incarnation."]],[2076,["He never told His father. He never told his mother."]],[2079,["He never told anybody that He was an incarnation."]],[2082,["Of course it was evident that he was."]],[2088,["His brother knew about it. Now he had two brothers."]],[2093,["Very interesting. I mean he had other brothers also,"]],[2096,["but Bharat and another was Lakshmana."]],[2099,["These two brothers were with him."]],[2101,["Now they show the two sides of a human being."]],[2105,["One was Lakshmana and he was that fiery type, you see."]],[2109,["He couldn’t bear anybody misbehaving towards Rama."]],[2113,["He couldn’t bear anybody talking in a very mundane type to Shri Rama."]],[2119,["And he used to get so angry with all these people"]],[2124,["that he would just come out like a big thunderbolt"]],[2128,["on anybody who tried to say anything about Shri Rama."]],[2134,["Even Parashurama, who was there,"]],[2138,["a contemporary incarnation of Shri Rama Himself was Parashurama."]],[2142,["It’s a very interesting story about that."]],[2144,["But, he could not bare Parashurama in any way…"]],[2149,["(break in recording)"]],[2154,["…He is the Shesha as they call it."]],[2159,["The serpent which sleeps in the bhavasagara."]],[2166,["On which Shri Vishnu rests."]],[2169,["The same Shesha had taken birth as Shri Lakshmana."]],[2173,["Now for a western mind, to them, snakes are sort of…"]],[2179,["if you talk about snakes for them, only they know"]],[2181,["the Adam and Eve snake that’s all,"]],[2183,["they don’t understand anything."]],[2185,["And they can’t understand why people worship snakes."]],[2189,["You see, snakes are, like cobra and all that, they are like the kings."]],[2194,["They are the kings of the underground."]],[2198,["And Shesha is the one who supports the whole Universe."]],[2204,["So this Shesha is worshipped"]],[2206,["as the cobras are worshipped in many villages in India, even today,"]],[2211,["because they don’t trouble anyone there."]],[2213,["Because they are like deities, are worshipped in India."]],[2216,["And sometimes they do, but mostly they do not bite a good religious man."]],[2224,["There’s a story of Sai Nath"]],[2230,["where a snake charmer"]],[2237,["was given a lot of money just to kill Shri Sai Nath."]],[2242,["And because Sai Nath, used to, in the night,"]],[2245,["suddenly goes up to his own swing he had made,"]],[2250,["about thirty feet above the ground."]],[2253,["God knows, nobody knew how he used to go there."]],[2256,["But they would find him sleeping up there. (Laughs)."]],[2259,["So this snake was taken by this snake charmer"]],[2265,["and he put the snake on to Sai Nath."]],[2270,["And the snake went there, and Sai Nath talked to him and He said,"]],[2274,["“Oh God, you’ve come here to meet me after such a long time."]],[2279,["What is your job?”"]],[2281,["He said, “This horrible snake charmer has asked me to bite you."]],[2284,["So I’ve come to tell you to be careful about these people.”"]],[2287,["The snake charmer was looking with amazement that he was talking to him!"]],[2292,["He said, “Alright, you go now.” He talked to him."]],[2294,["These are age-old snakes, you see."]],[2296,["So the snake went and bit the snake charmer."]],[2301,["But then he came down you see, from his thing,"]],[2305,["and he sucked his poison and threw it away."]],[2309,["“Because, after all, you see,” he said, “the snake is angry with you"]],[2313,["because you tried such a trick.” So he sucked in."]],[2315,["That’s compassion. That’s compassion."]],[2317,["And he sucked his venom out and the fellow was completely changed"]],[2324,["and he said, “Now I’m going to announce it to all the people"]],[2328,["what, these brahmins tried to kill,”"]],[2333,["that they wanted to kill Shri Sai Nath."]],[2336,["And why? Why were they so frightened of this man?"]],[2339,["He used to live outside the village"]],[2341,["and they were so frightened of him because they were doing all wrong things"]],[2345,["in the name of God. So they were all frightened that they’ll be exposed."]],[2350,["So, this is what it is, that He sleeps on the Shesha."]],[2354,["And Shesha is the one who is sometimes expressed in Sahaja Yogis,"]],[2359,["I have seen, as anger, when you try to be non protocolish"]],[2364,["or when you try to be funny or you don’t behave yourself."]],[2369,["That’s the Shesha in them."]],[2371,["That is also sometimes needed."]],[2373,["You have to be a Shesha sometimes because"]],[2376,["otherwise people will start misbehaving"]],[2379,["and by that they will be harmed."]],[2381,["Not that I will be harmed, but they will be harmed."]],[2383,["So that kind of temperament is also needed."]],[2386,["But the other one is very interesting, is that of Bharata, the brother."]],[2391,["He showed how Shri Rama bestowed the kingdom to him"]],[2395,["because of his mother’s agitation."]],[2400,["And he didn’t know what to do."]],[2405,["So he went back to Rama and he said that, “You take back your kingdom."]],[2409,["I don’t want anything. You are the one who should govern."]],[2412,["Why should I have it?”"]],[2415,["So Rama said, “Alright, you just be there in charge of the kingdom."]],[2421,["I have to obey my father, I have to obey my mother"]],[2424,["because I have given them a promise.”"]],[2427,["So Shri Rama’s another great quality was once given a promise"]],[2434,["is to be kept."]],[2436,["This is another quality we have to have that,"]],[2439,["if you have promised anything, you have to keep it."]],[2444,["If you have said, “I will do this,”, you must do it."]],[2447,["You should not find out excuses to avoid it."]],[2450,["It’s absolutely an anti-God activity to avoid doing"]],[2454,["things that you have promised."]],[2457,["Your Deities will never be happy."]],[2459,["You must see that, whatever you have promised you must do."]],[2464,["Now, when Bharata was sent back by Him"]],[2468,["he said, “Alright, give me your sandals which I’ll take there."]],[2474,["And I’ll use them as if that’s the symbol of you being there.”"]],[2479,["And he put those sandals on the throne"]],[2482,["and he ruled that kingdom and looked after – Bharata."]],[2485,["Though when he was going to see Rama"]],[2489,["then Lakshmana saw him coming and he said, “Look at this!"]],[2493,["He’s coming here to invade you now! He has thrown you out of the kingdom"]],[2496,["and now he’s coming to invade you.”"]],[2498,["So this is also, I’ve seen, among Sahaja Yogis, is there,"]],[2501,["that the Sahaja Yogis who are like Shesha"]],[2505,["cannot see also the goodness of other Sahaja Yogis"]],[2509,["who are very good people, extremely sacrificing, nice people"]],[2515,["but their intentions are not understood, are misunderstood,"]],[2520,["which is a very sad thing."]],[2522,["You must see the intentions of another type of people also,"]],[2525,["who may not be so hot tempered, may not be so much angry"]],[2528,["but their intentions are very good."]],[2531,["They have come actually to ask for the sandals of Shri Rama."]],[2538,["So among this two type of people, I have seen"]],[2540,["there is always a misunderstanding going on."]],[2544,["So both the types of people should try to understand"]],[2547,["that we both are needed for Sahaja Yoga."]],[2550,["I cannot only do with one type of people."]],[2553,["We have to have both types of people"]],[2556,["who will look after both the styles of the thing."]],[2559,["But when you are dealing with others one should go as one."]],[2564,["For example, if a person is coming to Caxton Hall"]],[2571,["and he says something"]],[2575,["then you should weigh it whether he’s a new one or an old one."]],[2579,["If he’s a new one then you must show all gentleness, kindness,"]],[2584,["all kinds of exterior things which will please him."]],[2587,["The reason is: he’s not a realised soul,"]],[2589,["he doesn’t see your subtle thing."]],[2591,["What he sees is what you are, outside."]],[2595,["How you are dressed, how you talk to them, how you behave towards them."]],[2601,["All these things they see first of all."]],[2604,["They don’t see what you have got inside."]],[2607,["They can’t see your heart, they can’t feel your vibrations,"]],[2610,["so you have to be very kind to them, you have to be very sweet to them."]],[2614,["I received a letter from someone saying that “The Sahaja Yogis"]],[2618,["have been very, very rude to me and have been angry.”"]],[2621,["Like the other day, somebody came and was sitting at the back:"]],[2625,["they are trying to salvage, salvage what you call"]],[2630,["the people who are lost by the cults or whatever it is."]],[2633,["He was sitting at the back and when I said, “Come forward.”"]],[2636,["And and he didn’t come so you said, “You get out!”"]],[2638,["You should not say! Let me say. That time you should keep quiet."]],[2643,["Nobody should say, “Get out! If you are not going.”"]],[2645,["Because the thing is if we say,"]],[2651,["“We don’t care for people who are not humble!”"]],[2653,["Then they are going to be lost in any case."]],[2656,["Let us give them a fair chance."]],[2659,["Let us give them a fair chance to come into Sahaja Yoga;"]],[2662,["first by your behaviour."]],[2663,["Now, some people have a habit of, sort of talking to them"]],[2668,["a bit too much. They should not talk. That’s one thing I feel,"]],[2673,["that, while giving vibrations and all that,"]],[2675,["at the most you should ask, “Are you feeling any cool breeze?”"]],[2684,["in a very humble way. And this is another quality of Shri Rama,"]],[2688,["is a sankoch. There’s no word in English language"]],[2692,["because you have ‘formality’"]],[2694,["which is a very insipid word to describe ‘ ‘sankoch’."]],[2698,["Because, there is no integration between your heart and formality."]],[2701,["But if you can think of a ‘formality of the heart’"]],[2704,["then what do you call that?"]],[2710,["What will you call in English language?"]],[2715,["The formality of the heart."]],[2718,["Yogini: Sincerity."]],[2720,["Shri Mataji: No, sincerity is different. It’s an action."]],[2725,["Sincerity is an abstract thing. But formality, from the heart."]],[2731,["You see, how to say such a thing?"]],[2736,["Yogini: ‘Honestly’ Mother. ‘Honestly’."]],[2741,["Shri Mataji: No, no. Not ‘honesty’. These are all abstract words."]],[2746,["In action."]],[2748,["You see, say for example, now, I am sitting."]],[2751,["Now if they bring me a cup, alright?"]],[2754,["It’s a broken cup, for example, you go to somebody’s house,"]],[2757,["and it’s a little broken."]],[2759,["So, if an Indian is there -I don’t know about Western style"]],[2762,["– he will drink it off."]],[2764,["He will not say anything, “It’s broken,” or anything."]],[2767,["But maybe somebody might say, “It’s a broken cup!”"]],[2773,["Or say, you go to somebody’s house"]],[2776,["and you don’t like a colour scheme or something."]],[2782,["So for an Indian person it would be not proper"]],[2787,["to immediately say like that – for an Indian person."]],[2793,["You see, “formality of the heart”."]],[2797,["Not to say something in such a way that"]],[2803,["you touch the wrong side of the person is sankoch."]],[2809,["Now to such an extent Shri Rama had that there’s a good story"]],[2814,["– I think I had said it before also, but again I’ll repeat it to you –"]],[2818,["which is described in another Ramayana written by Tulsidasa."]],[2822,["Although Tulsidasa was not a Realised soul,"]],[2825,["but some points he has brought out very well."]],[2828,["He says that:"]],[2829,["Shri Rama was putting the arrows"]],[2840,["against the heads of Ravana."]],[2845,["And he had ten heads. And he had a boon that,"]],[2850,["every head that falls off, another head will come up."]],[2853,["He had a boon like that. So his brother says,"]],[2855,["“What are you doing? You know that he cannot die"]],[2859,["by putting the arrows across his head."]],[2863,["You have to put it in his heart otherwise he will not die.”"]],[2866,["So the sankocha comes in Him and He said,"]],[2869,["“See, in his heart he has got my wife"]],[2873,["because he loves Her and She’s sitting in his heart."]],[2876,["How can I hit him in the heart? She’ll be hurt.”"]],[2879,["See the delicacy of his understanding."]],[2883,["So he said, “Then by hitting his head is he going to be killed?”"]],[2887,["He said, “You see, attention, once it going towards his head,"]],[2892,["his attention will be withdrawn from his heart."]],[2895,["And once the attention is withdrawn,"]],[2897,["my wife will not be there any more,"]],[2899,["then Ill hit him and I’ll kill him.”"]],[2904,["So see, the sankoch! You see, then you will understand that"]],[2907,["how we are rude and arrogant."]],[2912,["This kind of arrogance and rudeness comes to us because we have no sankoch."]],[2921,["We should not say everything to everyone. We need not."]],[2925,["Should we say everything? Say, for example, in your puja"]],[2929,["maybe you are doing something which should not be done."]],[2932,["I know it’s wrong. Unless and until it’s absolutely wrong,"]],[2935,["I will not tell. I said, “Gradually they will learn.”"]],[2938,["Because otherwise you become like this, you see, tensed up."]],[2941,["You must see Linda’s face if I tell her anything! She goes into…"]],[2947,["So that sankocha, that understanding comes if you love someone"]],[2953,["and understand. Now, you have to love all the seekers of the world."]],[2957,["They have done wrong, they have done all kinds of ego-trips,"]],[2959,["they have done all kinds of mistakes but your Mother loves them"]],[2963,["and you have to love them."]],[2965,["If they are to be corrected I’ll do that."]],[2969,["You just don’t do that way that they feel hurt."]],[2971,["Put a sankocha."]],[2974,["While talking to each other educate yourself,"]],[2977,["train yourself to say things which are sweet and nice,"]],[2984,["which will make another person feel"]],[2988,["that this person is a properly brought up person"]],[2993,["in Sahaja Yoga tradition."]],[2995,["So we have a Sahaja Yoga tradition also,"]],[2997,["in which, when we speak to each other,"]],[3000,["we have that sankocha within us of Shri Rama."]],[3004,["And if you do not have that sankocha"]],[3006,["you get the Right Heart."]],[3008,["And that Right Heart is a very dangerous thing in a country like England,"]],[3014,["where the climate is so bad,"]],[3016,["because it gives you a horrible thing like asthma."]],[3022,["I’m not frightening you, but it’s true."]],[3026,["You get asthma if your Right Heart is caught."]],[3029,["Not necessarily that asthma comes from Right Heart only"]],[3032,["– can also come from centre heart –"]],[3034,["but [if] you get Right Heart you definitely get asthma."]],[3038,["So the attitude you see, like your father."]],[3042,["I’ve heard people talking to father also in such a funny way."]],[3046,["You can’t talk to your father like that."]],[3048,["They talk to me also very rudely."]],[3050,["I mean, I have seen people, Sahaja Yogis, shockingly sometimes"]],[3054,["– on a very mundane level or you can say in a very unprotocolish way."]],[3060,["you will get into Right Heart."]],[3062,["So this sankoch one has to learn,"]],[3065,["the maryada: means the boundaries of your relationships."]],[3070,["You see, “we love each other,” doesn’t mean"]],[3072,["that we go on aggressing other’s privacies."]],[3077,["To what extent you love each other doesn’t mean"]],[3081,["that you go on in way that you try to transgress"]],[3085,["all the beauties and all the privacies of another person."]],[3090,["You see, [if] someone walks into the bedroom directly"]],[3093,["is not the way Sahaja Yoga should be. I need not tell."]],[3097,["But you must knock if you have to."]],[3098,["And knock at a time when you need it!"]],[3100,["All the time to knock or to hang onto someone all the time is not proper."]],[3106,["The sankocha is a complete cultural stuff."]],[3110,["So we have a cultural tradition which we have to learn from Shri Ram."]],[3117,["He’s known for his sankocha. Every time, how to say this,"]],[3121,["I cannot say that. We have this very much engrained within us."]],[3129,["The children are to be educated in that way,"]],[3132,["and once they are educated that way they will learn the sankoch,"]],[3137,["and that will give them a proper understanding of social life."]],[3144,["Like you now see, this light is here: if you put your finger to it,"]],[3148,["it might burn and you may remove your finger."]],[3151,["But if you are with another person"]],[3153,["and if you try to take liberties with that person"]],[3156,["a day may come when that person will misbehave"]],[3159,["or will harm you or do something to you. But still you will not realise"]],[3163,["[that] it is because you have no sankoch [that] it has happened."]],[3167,["So this sankoch has to be worked out very beautifully in every way:"]],[3172,["in thanks-giving, in accepting some body’s gratitude,"]],[3177,["in expressing your love to another person"]],[3180,["– in a way that is a sankoch."]],[3185,["Now Shri Rama is known for his boundaries."]],[3190,["He doesn’t cross the limit. Yesterday, the other day I told you about"]],[3195,["food, that you don’t cross the boundaries of food,"]],[3198,["like being compassionate to the bugs and to the mosquitoes."]],[3203,["In the same way in every thing discretion of the heart should be there."]],[3209,["Now, there is no word for “discretion of the heart”"]],[3214,["in the English language, which is maryada."]],[3217,["Discretion of the heart is, to understand, say, example,"]],[3227,["that if you are rude to your father what do you gain?"]],[3230,["You gain nothing. But if you are humble you might gain over,"]],[3234,["with your father alright. Even if he’s a bad man!"]],[3238,["Because what happens in reaction, if you say psychologically:"]],[3242,["Supposing you are the son of a father who is doing something wrong"]],[3247,["and you are obedient to him,"]],[3250,["he will always have a fear that he will lose you if he falls in your ideals."]],[3256,["So by that humility you will raise him."]],[3265,["If you are humble, if your behaviour towards your parents"]],[3268,["is like Shri Rama’s, there’s nothing to lose."]],[3271,["You don’t compromise in your principles or anything."]],[3274,["In day to day things, like that, [if] your father is sitting…"]],[3278,["I mean in India if the father is there,"]],[3280,["you won’t sit down before him, you won’t sit, at any cost."]],[3284,["Till he tells you ten times, you won’t sit before him."]],[3287,["It helps, you know. Then it reacts on the father"]],[3290,["that,  “Supposing I misbehave much my son will not respect me.”"]],[3296,["So the sense of respect also comes from your heart."]],[3300,["That’s only possible if you know that maryada from your heart"]],[3307,["how far to go. What is the need to be rude to your father?"]],[3310,["No need at all, at any cost! What is the need?"]],[3314,["Or to your husband or to your wife?"]],[3317,["Why to say anything harsh to anyone? What is the need?"]],[3320,["What are you going to gain out of it?"]],[3322,["By saying anything harsh I have not seen people have improved."]],[3325,["Only when a guru is harsh or,"]],[3329,["I mean, the mother or father are harsh to the children it helps."]],[3333,["Nowhere else it helps you in common relationships."]],[3336,["Like brothers and sisters, it does not, and higher and lower."]],[3342,["The lower person have to bear the harshness of the elders"]],[3345,["if they want to improve. There’s nothing!"]],[3347,["After all they’re not going to throttle you."]],[3350,["Supposing even if he says something bad to you – doesn’t matter."]],[3353,["You try to. And there, what one has to remember [is]"]],[3355,["what Christ has said that, you must put another cheek."]],[3360,["So use the heart’s discretion – how far to go to a person."]],[3365,["In the effect of it you will be a very, very powerful person,"]],[3370,["in your family, in Sahaja Yoga, anywhere."]],[3374,["Those people who are obedient to me are very powerful Sahaja Yogis."]],[3379,["You know that."]],[3382,["And those who are not go down very fast."]],[3386,["I try to save them, by everything, but I have seen"]],[3390,["– those who are disobedient, who don’t listen to me,"]],[3394,["who are rude to me, who do not understand the protocol,"]],[3397,["go down very much in Sahaja Yoga."]],[3399,["Absolutely (clicking fingers) like that!"]],[3401,["In a second I find they are going hundreds of feet down. It’s true."]],[3408,["Because what is lacking in you is the discretion, the maryada"]],[3412,["– how far to go. And that’s another thing we have to learn"]],[3416,["to educate ourselves."]],[3418,["So the education of Shri Rama as it was, I told you, that"]],[3422,["he could kill a demon with one arrow."]],[3425,["You don’t have to beat them a hundred and eight times,"]],[3429,["one beating should be sufficient."]],[3433,["But you have to be powerful people"]],[3435,["and the power of a person increases by putting maryada."]],[3440,["Supposing you have wheat, and you just spread it,"]],[3444,["it will spread all over, anybody will, birds will come and eat it off,"]],[3448,["it will be finished. But if you put them in a sack"]],[3452,["it will have a weight, it will have a size, it will rise in height"]],[3459,["and it is useful. It will have respect."]],[3462,["But the thing that is all spread all over, which has no maryada,"]],[3466,["will never be respected."]],[3468,["Nothing works out without maryada. Even the light keeps to a maryada."]],[3474,["You have to keep your maryadas. That is part of our training, you see."]],[3479,["Say, for example, an aeroplane is there"]],[3483,["and it is not bound by any maryadas."]],[3485,["You see, it is not bound. When it goes in the air"]],[3489,["it will be all finished!"]],[3491,["All our ideas of freedom are to be bound by maryada."]],[3497,["If the freedom has no maryada it is abandonment,"]],[3501,["it is nonsense, it is not going to help us."]],[3505,["So we have to create out of Sahaja Yogis great politicians."]],[3509,["It has been predicted that if Sahaja Yoga does not spread"]],[3515,["then the third world war is inevitable."]],[3518,["People will suffer a lot with a third world war."]],[3521,["It is possible to avoid it if people take to Sahaja Yoga in a big number."]],[3528,["But if they do not, there will be a third world war"]],[3531,["and the effects of that will harm people so much"]],[3534,["that ultimately it is the Sahaja Yogis who will be called for a conference"]],[3539,["and not the diplomats."]],[3541,["The Sahaja Yogis will be consulted,"]],[3543,["and they will decide what is to be done for the world"]],[3546,["and they will become the rulers of tomorrow’s world."]],[3550,["So we must have a full idea [of] how to be rulers like Shri Rama."]],[3556,["We have to go too far with ourselves, to training up ourselves,"]],[3560,["educating ourselves, getting rid of our egos"]],[3563,["and understanding that we have to grow."]],[3567,["It’s a very big task, it’s a great task and sometimes you might think,"]],[3571,["“How can Mother expect us to do it?”"]],[3574,["But I think you are the people who are chosen for it"]],[3577,["and you have to get to it and work it out."]],[3579,["So we have to train up ourselves to be first good rulers of ourselves"]],[3583,["and the rulers of others."]],[3585,["First we must learn to rule ourselves. You see,"]],[3588,["here in this body only you’ll learn how to rule yourself."]],[3593,["Comfort, if you get fond of comfort,"]],[3596,["make your body work it out that there’s no comfort needed."]],[3601,["If your body indulges into too much eating or anything,"]],[3604,["make your body learn that it’s not good to indulge into it."]],[3608,["If you speak too much, talk too much, if you are rude,"]],[3611,["just say that, “I’m not going to say a word from morning till evening.”"]],[3614,["Take to mauna (silence). So the tapah, is the penance time,"]],[3619,["is now ahead of us."]],[3621,["With that penance, the greatest thing that is going to help you"]],[3625,["is to go and talk of Sahaja Yoga – give the message of my advent –"]],[3632,["and also talk about how the transformation, the blossom time has come."]],[3637,["This you have to do, plus you have to learn how to rule yourself"]],[3642,["and then how to rule others through your heart, not through your mind."]],[3646,["You have to rule through your hearts by learning all the qualities"]],[3650,["of the heart which I have told you."]],[3652,["And I must congratulate you for the article you have written on Blossom Time."]],[3656,["I have gone through it. I have really enjoyed it, thoroughly."]],[3659,["He’s done very well. May God bless you!"]],[3661,["And I think it will have a good [effect]…"]],[3663,["I’m surprised how they published it:"]],[3665,["have they changed their mind or what happened?"]],[3668,["It’s amazing! Have you seen that article?"]],[3671,["It’s great."]],[3677,["And thank you very much for the nice creepers you have sent me."]],[3683,["They are so beautiful you see, they still are under a shock"]],[3686,["because I removed them from your gentle care to mine."]],[3690,["And mine is a little sort of flippant one now."]],[3693,["But today we tried to do some justice to them."]],[3695,["I’m sure they’ll. We gave them a bandhan."]],[3702,["Shri Mataji: You mean you want to be more intelligent?"]],[3705,["Yogi: No, to get rid of the rubbish Mother."]],[3707,["Shri Mataji: Rubbish that is in the head?"]],[3710,["You see, the best one, in Sanskrit it is said,"]],[3712,["“Ya neti neti wachane nigamor avochus.”"]],[3715,["means, you go on telling your mind, “This is not, this is not, this is not.”"]],[3720,["Any thought that comes to your mind, you go on telling,"]],[3722,["“this is not the thought. Not this, not this, not this.”"]],[3728,["Then the inspiration starts coming."]],[3731,["You see, what I feel, people are not inspired."]],[3735,["They have got fear on one side."]],[3738,["Suddenly, you do something to them they go into a fear, a trauma."]],[3741,["Or else, if you try to be good to them, they go into an ego-trip."]],[3747,["So to stay in the centre, what you have to do,"]],[3749,["is to go on saying “Not this thought,” and, “not this thought.”"]],[3752,["Then you will be a deep Sahaja Yogi."]],[3756,["Best is this. Because intellect is nothing – so-called intellect."]],[3759,["Only God has intelligence, nobody has! To be very frank."]],[3769,["It’s a big joke, isn’t it?"]],[3772,["Every one thinks they are intelligent but they are not, they are stupid."]],[3776,["You see, all stupidity is considered as intelligence these days."]],[3780,["For example, cunningness – it never pays you dividends."]],[3783,["What is intellect? Is the only understanding of intellect"]],[3788,["as Adi Shankaracharya had put it –"]],[3793,["“Na yoge, na sankhya,”"]],[3795,["All these things are good for nothing."]],[3797,["Only service to your Mother is the best way."]],[3802,["Ask your intellect, “Is it serving my Mother?”"]],[3807,["Intellect will tell you, the so-called intellect of human beings,"]],[3811,["to cheat yourself. It cheats you. It gives you escapes. It cheats you."]],[3816,["All the time the intellect is working by saying,"]],[3819,["“This may be good, that may be good” you see,"]],[3822,["but the real good, it never sees."]],[3825,["It’s a trick of the ego, trick of the ego."]],[3829,["Is the choices. Ego likes choices, you see."]],[3832,["So, “This is good, this is bad, this I don’t like this, this.”"]],[3836,["All ‘I’ business should be given up and say that,"]],[3839,["“Not this, not this, not this.”"]],[3843,["“We” should come in, “we”, not “I”."]],[3848,["Now you are not anymore ‘I’s, you are ‘we’ now."]],[3856,["That’s how the intellect will go away."]],[3858,["Because this intellect has gathered all kind of nonsense"]],[3861,["and it doesn’t exist! That’s the biggest maya!"]],[3863,["It doesn’t exist! There is no intelligence at all!"]],[3867,["What is the intelligence, is just to understand"]],[3870,["that there is nothing like this intellect – you are nothing."]],[3876,["You see, to explain His intellect would be something"]],[3879,["like explaining human civilisation to an ant!"]],[3882,["Even that is easier! It’s like that – His intellect."]],[3891,["And He’s innocent. So simple. I mean, anybody is amazed how can that be."]],[3900,["So the most intelligent person is the one who knows"]],[3907,["that our intellect is just a ego-trip."]],[3915,["This is the sign of pure intelligence,"]],[3920,["is the sign of pure understanding"]],[3926,["that the heart is the ruler, there resides the Spirit"]],[3932,["which is the most intelligent thing within us."]],[3937,["And the inspiration of the Spirit is the manifestation"]],[3942,["of the pure intellect of God."]],[3947,["And what I told you today is the intellect of the heart."]],[3954,["But of the brain – zero!"]],[3961,["But then, what’s the use of the brain?"]],[3964,["Why have brain? Why not only have heart? It would be alright."]],[3968,["But the brain is the one which acts."]],[3971,["Heart gives the inspiration but the brain acts on it,"]],[3976,["it’s communicating."]],[3979,["But the inspiration, the source, is the heart, is the Spirit."]],[3983,["Again connect yourself to the Spirit."]],[3990,["Intelligently, how will you explain Kundalini awakening?"]],[3998,["Leave alone Kundalini, how can you explain sprouting of the seed"]],[4002,["intelligently, through your intellect?"]],[4006,["Explain, means, explain why, how."]],[4016,["Sprouting of the seed, a simple thing"]],[4018,["which you see thousand and one times."]],[4023,["How will you explain? Intellect is that says, “I cannot explain.”"]],[4031,["A very limited thing. It’s ego, nothing but ego."]],[4040,["And once you get rid of it then the pure intellect starts coming in."]],[4045,["You see, with [Mr.] Yoga Singh, you will be amazed, you see, who is,"]],[4049,["I mean he came to us as a bhoot absolutely. He’s so much changed."]],[4053,["Now he speaks, I tell you, he speaks like a saint."]],[4056,["I was amazed!"]],[4061,["He speaks so well sometimes that I want to quote him sometimes"]],[4064,["– the way he speaks about certain things."]],[4066,["I am amazed how he has started talking like that."]],[4074,["So whatever you have to say relate it to the Spirit"]],[4077,["you will talk like saints."]],[4079,["Relate it to Spirit, not to anything else,"]],[4083,["relate it to Spirit and you will be amazed."]],[4093,["He told me that, “There are many people in this world who are absurd.”"]],[4098,["I said, “How do you know?”"]],[4100,["He says “Because they don’t want to know anything about you."]],[4107,["I don’t know why are they here and why have you created them!”"]],[4114,["You see, he was a person with so many bhoots on his head."]],[4122,["He’s such a beautiful man, I tell you."]],[4125,["He says this, “This is your servant is alright,"]],[4128,["but he has to learn certain things if he has to live well."]],[4132,["He doesn’t have neatness. Because his mind is not neat."]],[4139,["He has to be a cleaner person. But his mind is not clean."]],[4144,["His heart is alright. But the mind should be clean.”"]],[4149,["I was amazed at him."]],[4153,["He’s not an educated man or anything, just an ordinary person."]],[4157,["But they start talking like prophets."]],[4160,["I think you’d better read some of the prophets"]],[4162,["you will also start talking like them."]],[4165,["You read Kabir, Khalil Gibran, all these people."]],[4170,["What is Blake? He was a prophet too."]],[4174,["You can talk like him. Why not?"]],[4178,["He talked through his Spirit isn’t it? Pure intelligence."]],[4184,["Then you’ll become Shri Rama if you can do that."]],[4190,["So today’s a great day. I’m happy you all could come."]],[4194,["And it has worked out so well that this is,"]],[4198,["I was going to come here and talk about Shri Rama"]],[4203,["and wish you all that you follow Him up."]],[4209,["Respect yourself!"]],[4210,["And it’s your responsibility to be good, to be like that,"]],[4215,["to work it out that way."]],[4219,["May God bless you."]],[4239,["Alright.  You wanted to do a small, little puja? You can wash my feet."]],[4244,["And have you got Shri Rama’s anything"]],[4253,["Gavin Brown reads from “Ramayana of Valmiki”, Chapter 86"]]]);
